Here's a detailed list format of the technical and cyber due diligence checklists:


---

Technical Due Diligence Checklist

1. Technology Stack

Review primary programming languages, frameworks, and databases.

Assess legacy systems and technical debt.



2. Architecture

Evaluate scalability and flexibility of the architecture.

Assess cloud vs. on-premise infrastructure and hybrid configurations.

Review microservices architecture, if applicable.



3. Code Quality

Conduct a code review to assess quality, consistency, and adherence to best practices.

Measure code technical debt and reusability.



4. Development Process

Review development methodologies (Agile, Scrum, etc.).

Evaluate use of CI/CD (Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment).



5. Product Roadmap

Assess short and long-term product development plans.

Analyze innovation and differentiation in the product pipeline.



6. Third-Party Dependencies

List third-party software libraries, APIs, and services.

Evaluate license agreements and compatibility (e.g., open-source software compliance).



7. Testing

Review unit, integration, and regression testing coverage.

Evaluate automated testing and QA processes.



8. Documentation

Review code documentation, product manuals, and knowledge base.



9. Data Architecture

Examine data models, schema design, and relationships.

Assess data management practices (archiving, backups, replication).



10. Integration Capability

Assess API availability and quality, including REST and/or GraphQL.
